---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import StudioImage from "../../components/StudioImage.astro";
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" page="classes" title="Classes">
  <h1>Classes</h1>

  <section id="foundational">
    <h2><a href="/en/schedule/#foundational">Kunga Yoga Flow</a></h2>
    <StudioImage
      src='/images/classes/yoga-class-siva-darsana-400.webp'
      alt="Śivadarśana"
      thumbnail="lg"
      class="thumbnail-right"
    />
    <p>
      Kunga Yoga Flow classes link breath and movement in creative sequences that work all of the major joints and muscles of the body and incorporate extended holds. This class is open to all levels and accessible to any and all body types. Posture (Āsana) alignment, meditation, breathing techniques (Prāṇāyāma), movement, and mindfulness are introduced. Use props to support your poses. Feel comfortable in the foundational postures that are offered.
    </p>
    <p>
      Kunga Yoga is a service-oriented non-lineage style of yoga for all people of all backgrounds, shapes, sizes, and abilities. „Kunga“ is a Rwandan word meaning „to help or to serve“. Please take personal responsibility for your safety and your needs, honoring your practice in the way that suits you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Kunga Yoga classes support service work. A portion of proceeds from Kunga Yoga classes supports charitable projects chosen by the Kunga community.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/en/schedule">Book a Class</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="26+2">
    <h2><a href="/en/schedule/#26+2">26+2 (Non-Heated)</a></h2>
    <StudioImage
      src='/images/classes/yoga-natarajasana-400.webp'
      alt="Naṭarājāsana (Standing Bow)"
      thumbnail="md"
      class="thumbnail-right"
    />
    <p>
      A steady, meditative practice following the classic 26 postures and 2 breathing exercises.<br />
      Taught at room temperature, this version offers all the structure, clarity, and focus of the traditional sequence without the intensity of heat. Offered in 60-minute (Express) and 90-minute (Classic) formats.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ideal for anyone who wants to learn the postures, build strength, and balance progressively, or experience the grounding rhythm of 26+2 in a calm, accessible environment.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you’d like to see a <a href="/en/contact/?interest=heated-26+2">heated 26+2</a> in the future, feel free to share your interest.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/en/schedule">Book a Class</a></p>
  </section>

  <section id="yin">
    <h2><a href="/en/schedule/#yin">Yin / Restorative</a></h2>
    <p>
      A slow, grounding, deeply supportive practice.<br />
      If you’d like to see <a href="/en/contact/?interest=yin">Yin</a> on the weekly schedule, let us know — we add new classes based on community interest. Slow, grounding, and supportive practice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="barre">
    <h2><a href="/en/schedule/#barre">Barre</a></h2>
    <p>
      Strength, alignment, rhythm, and mindful conditioning.<br />
      <a href="/en/contact/?interest=barre">Barre</a> classes can be added to the schedule when there is enough interest. Tell us if you’d join.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="meditation">
    <h2><a href="/en/schedule/#meditation">Meditation</a></h2>
    <p>
      A quiet, guided space to settle, breathe, and reconnect.<br />
      <a href="/en/contact/?interest=meditation">Meditation</a> sessions are offered when there is community demand. Share your interest anytime.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="next-steps">
    <h2>Book a Class</h2>
    <p>
      When you’re ready to schedule, you can book a class directly through Mindbody.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="button" href="/en/schedule">
        Book a Class
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
